  "articleBody": "Hiring a handyman can be incredibly helpful for those smaller tasks and repairs, but there are a few common pitfalls you'll want to avoid to ensure a smooth project. One frequent mistake is having an unclear scope of work. You might think you've explained it, but without a clear definition, expectations can get misaligned. Always make sure you and your handyman are on the same page about exactly what needs to be done. Another issue is underestimating the cost of parts or labor. It's easy to think a job will be quick and cheap, but unforeseen issues can arise. This leads to another pitfall: skipping a written estimate. Always get a clear estimate that outlines the work and costs, so there are no surprises down the line. Finally, a big mistake is assuming a handyman can handle work that actually requires a licensed specialist or permit review. While handymen are versatile, jobs involving electrical, plumbing, structural elements, or anything that changes permitted systems might need a specialized pro and potentially a permit. Clarifying this upfront can save you headaches later. At HH Remodeling LLC, we believe in open communication and transparent pricing to make sure your handyman experience is stress-free and successful. If you're unsure whether your project falls into handyman territory or needs a specialist, just ask!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
